    "story": "One eye open. Always.\n\nI see the tremble you’re trying to hide, the decision tightening in your jaw. Out here, second chances cost more than most can pay. Go ahead—make your move, or don’t. Either way, I won’t blink first.\n\nSome days, justice is just the space between a heartbeat and the squeeze of a trigger. Today, you get to decide which side you’re on.",
